const outlineTasks = `[{key:"meta",count:2+context.section_count,maxLength:160,instruction:"Plan the WHOLE article now. Line 1: title, at most 8 words and 100 characters. Line 2: angle, at most 12 words. Then exactly "+context.section_count+" DISTINCT headings in order, at most 4 words and 80 characters each. Each heading must cover a different reader need, never synonyms for an earlier topic. First: direct answer. Last: next steps for the requested decision, not a related process from a source. Match the exact reader intent in context.topic. Plan coverage using the evidence, not repeated filler. For a hiring, buying or decision guide, dedicate most headings to comparing options, checking suitability, questions, costs, agreements and practical next steps. Subject background gets at most one heading. Do not turn the guide into a subject overview. Keep conditions attached to the named service or group; listing criteria are not universal requirements. Do not require facts that the evidence cannot support. At most 75 words total.",existing:original?[original.title,original.angle,...original.sections.map(s=>s.heading)]:[]},...Array.from({length:context.section_count},(_,i)=>({key:"section",index:i,count:2,maxLength:110,instruction:"Requirements for section "+(i+1)+" of "+context.section_count+", budget "+context.budgets[i]+" words. The assigned heading is fixed by the full article plan. Return only two concise requirements, at most 14 words each. Do not repeat other sections' coverage. "+(i===0?"Start with a useful direct answer.":i===context.section_count-1?"Conclude with practical next steps; do not introduce new facts.":"Cover this heading's distinct reader need."),existing:original?original.sections[i].points:[]}))]`;
